Replace ``pkg_resources`` namespace with PEP 420 native namespace. Support Plone 6.0, 6.1, and Plone 6.2 on Python 3.10+. When you use ``collective.upgrade`` with other packages in the ``collective`` namespace, and you get a ``ModuleNotFoundError``, you may need to install ``horse-with-no-namespace``, or use ``zc.buildout`` 5.
[szakitibi] (plone/Products.CMFPlone#3928)

Drop support for Python 2 and Python 3 versions older than 3.10.
[szakitibi]

Drop support for Plone <6.0 including the replacement or cleanup of the Archetypes, portal_quickinstaller, resourceregistry, CMFEditionsFolderMigrator, collective.setdefaulteditor related code.
[laulaz, szakitibi]

Rework CSV import/export to use py3 io, with explicit UTF-8 encoding and close the reader.
[szakitibi]

Replace no longer supported ``scripts=["run-portal-upgrades"]`` with ``console_scripts``, fix missing ``Manager`` role.
[szakitibi]

Fix missing ``@@plone-addsite`` case for Plone 6.1+ - see plone/Products.CMFPlone#3981.
[szakitibi]

Portal_properties is no longer a persistent tool.
[bsuttor]
